# M9 walkthrough: model prices, task cards with tokens and cost, and the usage report.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisites: a provider and a default model (m1-providers.http), a department with a lead.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@providerId = paste-a-provider-id
@departmentId = paste-a-department-id
@taskId = paste-a-task-id

### What a model costs, USD per million tokens (cached input: the input price when left out).
### Calls are priced as they happen: a price set now doesn't reprice earlier calls.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers/{{providerId}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "modelId": "your-model-id", "inputUsd": 0.5, "cachedInputUsd": 0.05, "outputUsd": 1.5 }

### The provider's models, with their prices.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers/{{providerId}}/models
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A task: its "usage" counts every call made for it (its lead's, its specialists', memory's).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The board: every card has its usage too.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/board?departmentId={{departmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tokens and cost by department (calls outside tasks, the chief's, under a null key).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/usage?group=department
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### By model, or agent, or task, or day (your timezone), over a period.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/usage?group=day&from=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One department's tasks only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/usage?group=task&departmentId={{departmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Traces: Mastra's own routes (Studio's Traces page reads them). A task's runs carry its id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/observability/traces?page=0&perPage=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
